description:
Write the kernel's counted string functions from lesson 1.03 (simplified versions of the `Rtl` functions):

```cpp
using NTSTATUS = std::int32_t;
constexpr NTSTATUS STATUS_SUCCESS = 0;
constexpr NTSTATUS STATUS_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL = static_cast<NTSTATUS>(0xC0000023u);
struct UNICODE_STRING { std::uint16_t Length; std::uint16_t MaximumLength; char16_t* Buffer; };

void initString(UNICODE_STRING& s, const char16_t* nullTerminated);       // RtlInitUnicodeString
void copyString(UNICODE_STRING& dest, const UNICODE_STRING& src);         // RtlCopyUnicodeString
NTSTATUS appendString(UNICODE_STRING& dest, const UNICODE_STRING& src);   // RtlAppendUnicodeStringToString
bool equalStrings(const UNICODE_STRING& a, const UNICODE_STRING& b, bool ignoreCase);
bool isPrefix(const UNICODE_STRING& prefix, const UNICODE_STRING& s, bool ignoreCase);
std::u16string toStd(const UNICODE_STRING& s);                            // only the first Length bytes
```

- **Lengths are in bytes.** `initString` points `Buffer` at the given text, sets `Length` to its length in bytes without the null, and `MaximumLength` to that plus 2. A null pointer gives an empty string (all zero).
- `copyString` copies as many whole characters as fit into `dest`'s buffer (`MaximumLength`), and sets `dest.Length`; if there is room for another character, it also writes a null after the copy (not counted in `Length`).
- `appendString` adds `src` after `dest`'s text if the result fits in `dest.MaximumLength`, else changes nothing and returns `STATUS_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL`.
- Case-insensitive comparison only needs to fold `a`-`z` to upper case here.

